Flow 1: https://apps.cloneops.ai/flows/6a357f312c1eebe7d32dff00 Why did the latest execution fail? It met all the criteria.

The root cause is clear. Here's exactly what's happening:

Root Cause: node-update-record — Wrong Key Variable

Node: Update Data Store RecordError: Record with key "undefined" not found

The node's key is set to:

=variables.resolvedRecordEmail.existingKey

But variables.resolvedRecordEmail is never populated — it's undefined. This means the key resolves to undefined, and the update fails because there's no record with that key.

This is a consistent bug — it has failed on every new application since at least Aug 3rd (10+ failures, all the same node, all the same error).

What the key should be

Looking at the input data flowing into the node, the record is a new applicant being written for the first time. The data store uses email as the key (based on how Flow 5 and Flow 2 look up records by email). The key should simply be:

=variables.applicantRecord.email

or, if this is an update path after a CREATE node, the key should reference whatever variable the preceding CREATE node stored the key in.

What to check in the flow

There are two scenarios depending on what node-prepare-record-email (the parent node) is supposed to do:

If this is a CREATE + UPDATE pattern — the CREATE node should write the record first (keyed by email), and the UPDATE node's key should be =variables.applicantRecord.email

If resolvedRecordEmail was a variable from a lookup node — that lookup node may have been removed or renamed, leaving this node referencing a stale variable name

The fix: In the Flow 1 editor, find the Update Data Store Record node (node-update-record) and change the key from:

=variables.resolvedRecordEmail.existingKey

to:

=variables.applicantRecord.email

This will correctly key the record by the applicant's email, which is consistent with how every other flow looks up and updates candidate records.



